    <string name="dark_hint">Dark capture: dial / 0.5s / 1s, 30 RAWs each. Cover lens.</string>
    <string name="dark_title">Dark-frame calibration</string>
    <string name="dark_instructions">Cover the Lucid lens completely with an opaque cap. Turning the room light off is not enough. Keep the camera warmed up at the target temperature.\n\nCaptures 30 RAWs each at dial exposure, 0.5s and 1s (90 frames, several minutes; allow about 2 GB free). Gain and HDR clamping are unchanged. White/NIR lights and depth are off during capture.\n\nSaves original RAWs and RGGB residual dark-signal estimates in JSON, without subtraction. Includes dark current; not a guaranteed sensor pedestal. Tap the shutter again to stop after the current frame.</string>
